{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a1-kids-daily-life-of-in-the-usa/audio/main-875fd039bea7.mp3","durationSec":314.736,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.98,"text":"It is early morning in an American home."},{"start":2.7,"end":4.36,"text":"A boy has little time before school."},{"start":5.08,"end":5.66,"text":"What does he eat?"},{"start":6.42,"end":7.72,"text":"Often, he eats cereal."},{"start":8.24,"end":10.36,"text":"He puts cereal in a bowl and adds milk."},{"start":10.98,"end":13,"text":"He does not cook, so it is fast."},{"start":13.96,"end":15.52,"text":"Cereal is a ready-to-eat food."},{"start":16.24,"end":17.8,"text":"It is common in Western countries."},{"start":18.28,"end":18.96,"text":"It is not new."},{"start":19.38,"end":21.6,"text":"People have eaten it since the late 19th century."},{"start":22.08,"end":23.06,"text":"It has a long history."},{"start":23.5,"end":24.04,"text":"Look at the box."},{"start":24.5,"end":26.14,"text":"It often has bright colors and cartoons."},{"start":26.14,"end":30.06,"text":"Companies often sell cereal to children, not only to parents."},{"start":30.06,"end":32.26,"text":"So the child helps choose breakfast."},{"start":32.26,"end":34.8,"text":"A company helps shape that choice."},{"start":35.58,"end":36.78,"text":"Is cereal a bad choice?"},{"start":37.28,"end":37.82,"text":"Not always."},{"start":38.54,"end":42.96,"text":"People who eat breakfast cereal regularly have lower risks of obesity and diabetes."},{"start":43.76,"end":46.02,"text":"So a fast breakfast can still be a good habit."},{"start":46.76,"end":49.56,"text":"A busy morning and a healthy morning can go together."},{"start":50.54,"end":51.78,"text":"Picture a street in the morning."},{"start":52.18,"end":53.6,"text":"A big yellow bus stops."},{"start":54.4,"end":55,"text":"Lights flash."},{"start":55,"end":56.38,"text":"Cars stop."},{"start":56.38,"end":57.54,"text":"Children get on."},{"start":58.02,"end":59.6,"text":"This is the American school bus."},{"start":60.14,"end":64.36,"text":"In the USA, yellow school buses carry students to school and home again."},{"start":64.88,"end":67.6,"text":"They also carry students to school trips and events."},{"start":68.34,"end":70.04,"text":"The bus has special safety parts."},{"start":70.82,"end":72.64,"text":"Warning lights tell other cars to stop."},{"start":73.24,"end":75.34,"text":"An alarm helps the driver check for children."},{"start":75.86,"end":77.66,"text":"No child must stay on the bus alone."},{"start":78.36,"end":80.88,"text":"Cameras catch cars that pass the bus in a bad way."},{"start":81.56,"end":82.72,"text":"Do these safety parts work?"},{"start":83.28,"end":83.48,"text":"Yes."},{"start":84.14,"end":87.34,"text":"School buses see only about five child deaths each year."},{"start":87.94,"end":91.06,"text":"They are over 70 times safer than a car ride to school."},{"start":91.76,"end":93.4,"text":"So parents do not need to drive."},{"start":94.06,"end":97.06,"text":"The bus is a public system, and it does a family job."},{"start":97.66,"end":98.88,"text":"The bus arrives at school."},{"start":99.56,"end":100.94,"text":"What schools do children go to?"},{"start":101.56,"end":103.66,"text":"Most US children go to public schools."},{"start":104.16,"end":107.64,"text":"They go to elementary school first, then middle school, then high school."},{"start":108.22,"end":111.18,"text":"The school day often has a break called recess."},{"start":111.64,"end":112.9,"text":"Children play in the yard."},{"start":112.9,"end":115.8,"text":"But some US schools are removing recess."},{"start":116.5,"end":118.88,"text":"This may be bad for children's health and behavior."},{"start":119.9,"end":123.86,"text":"So the school system is strong, but it is not the same in every school."},{"start":124.84,"end":127.18,"text":"At noon, look at two children at one table."},{"start":127.9,"end":129.62,"text":"One child opens a bag from home."},{"start":130.12,"end":132.52,"text":"The other child has a tray from the school kitchen."},{"start":133.34,"end":136.26,"text":"The bag from home often has a PB&J sandwich."},{"start":137.06,"end":139.26,"text":"PB&J means peanut butter and jelly."},{"start":139.83,"end":141.46,"text":"People put both on bread."},{"start":142.24,"end":144.28,"text":"Often it is white bread and grape jelly."},{"start":145.04,"end":147.06,"text":"It is a famous American comfort food."},{"start":147.74,"end":149.18,"text":"Many children eat it at school."},{"start":150,"end":151.38,"text":"The tray is a school meal."},{"start":152.36,"end":156.02,"text":"In the US, some schools give free meals to all students."},{"start":156.9,"end":159.68,"text":"Other schools give free meals only to poor families."},{"start":160.38,"end":162.94,"text":"So two schools can have two different rules."},{"start":163.88,"end":166.2,"text":"Free meals do more than fill a stomach."},{"start":167.04,"end":170.5,"text":"Some places have many families without enough food."},{"start":170.88,"end":173.78,"text":"In these places, free meals help school discipline."},{"start":174.4,"end":175.3,"text":"Students behave better."},{"start":175.9,"end":177.5,"text":"A hungry child cannot learn well."},{"start":178.02,"end":179.7,"text":"A full child can sit and listen."},{"start":180.38,"end":183.68,"text":"So lunch is part of learning, not only a break from learning."},{"start":184.6,"end":186.04,"text":"School ends in the afternoon."},{"start":186.64,"end":188.3,"text":"Many parents work later than that."},{"start":188.68,"end":189.5,"text":"So there is a gap."},{"start":190.22,"end":191.12,"text":"Where do the children go?"},{"start":191.92,"end":193.86,"text":"Many children go to after-school activities."},{"start":194.24,"end":198.02,"text":"They play sports, make art, or study with a coach or a teacher."},{"start":198.64,"end":200.68,"text":"An adult watches the children the whole time."},{"start":201.36,"end":202.72,"text":"This helps working parents."},{"start":203.36,"end":205.22,"text":"They can stay at work and not worry."},{"start":206.2,"end":207.9,"text":"These activities happen after school."},{"start":208.46,"end":210.56,"text":"They also happen on weekends and in summer."},{"start":211.36,"end":213.94,"text":"So they fill many gaps, not only one."},{"start":214.44,"end":215.52,"text":"They help children too."},{"start":216.08,"end":217.38,"text":"The activity is not only fun."},{"start":218.06,"end":221.54,"text":"It also gives children a safe place with an adult and a good group."},{"start":222.3,"end":223.86,"text":"Imagine a young girl named Emma."},{"start":224.4,"end":225.7,"text":"She eats dinner with her family."},{"start":226.14,"end":226.92,"text":"She does her homework."},{"start":227.74,"end":229.02,"text":"Then the evening slows down."},{"start":229.74,"end":230.78,"text":"Now bedtime starts."},{"start":231.86,"end":233.1,"text":"Bedtime is a routine."},{"start":233.82,"end":235.86,"text":"A routine is the same steps every night."},{"start":236.38,"end":238.2,"text":"Emma's parents help her get ready for sleep."},{"start":238.84,"end":240.02,"text":"She changes into pajamas."},{"start":240.6,"end":242.56,"text":"Her mother or father reads her a story."},{"start":243.34,"end":244.5,"text":"Sometimes they sing a song."},{"start":245.32,"end":246.8,"text":"Why do the same steps every night?"},{"start":247.42,"end":249.7,"text":"The steps tell the child, \"Sleep is coming.\""},{"start":250.36,"end":252.12,"text":"The parents guide each step."},{"start":253.28,"end":254.02,"text":"Look back at the day."},{"start":254.78,"end":256.16,"text":"A company sells the cereal."},{"start":256.66,"end":258.44,"text":"The school runs the bus and lunch."},{"start":259.02,"end":260.9,"text":"A coach watches the children after school."},{"start":261.38,"end":263.02,"text":"But at night, the family leads."},{"start":263.62,"end":264.84,"text":"Bedtime belongs to the parents."},{"start":265.28,"end":266.96,"text":"On Saturday, there is no school bus."},{"start":267.48,"end":268.54,"text":"There is no school lunch."},{"start":269.28,"end":270.34,"text":"Does the system stop?"},{"start":270.82,"end":271.3,"text":"Not always."},{"start":271.3,"end":274.26,"text":"After-school activities also happen on weekends."},{"start":274.96,"end":277.42,"text":"A child can have a game or a class on Saturday."},{"start":277.7,"end":279.44,"text":"An adult watches the children again."},{"start":280.24,"end":282.78,"text":"So the weekend is freer, but it is not empty."},{"start":283.64,"end":287.82,"text":"It has many of the same parts: a group, a place and an adult."},{"start":288.76,"end":289.76,"text":"This is the big picture."},{"start":290.72,"end":294.1,"text":"A US child's day is not only about family choice."},{"start":294.7,"end":296.5,"text":"Many parts come from bigger systems."},{"start":297.42,"end":298.92,"text":"A company makes the breakfast cereal."},{"start":299.54,"end":301.82,"text":"The public school has the bus and the meals."},{"start":301.82,"end":305.46,"text":"Programs watch children after school and on weekends."},{"start":306.28,"end":308.84,"text":"The family leads bedtime and some free time."},{"start":309.72,"end":312.04,"text":"These systems try to keep children safe and fed."},{"start":312.7,"end":314.2,"text":"They also give parents time to work."}],"words":[{"text":"It","start":0,"end":0.14},{"text":"is","start":0.14,"end":0.28},{"text":"early","start":0.28,"end":0.58},{"text":"morning","start":0.58,"end":0.9},{"text":"in","start":0.9,"end":1.18},{"text":"an","start":1.18,"end":1.3},{"text":"American","start":1.3,"end":1.58},{"text":"home","start":1.58,"end":1.98},{"text":"A","start":2.7,"end":2.72},{"text":"boy","start":2.72,"end":2.9},{"text":"has","start":2.9,"end":3.12},{"text":"little","start":3.12,"end":3.3},{"text":"time","start":3.3,"end":3.64},{"text":"before","start":3.64,"end":3.96},{"text":"school","start":3.96,"end":4.3